00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.750
<i>What should we do?</i>
<i>We're not used to facing adversity</i>

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.880
<i>So our resolve's definitely not all there</i>

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.290
<i>Back then, we were just</i>

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.630
<i>Envious of others and</i>

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:22.340
<i>Angry at something we couldn't see</i>

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.880
<i>We just kept glaring at the next step</i>

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.250
<i>That we could've easily taken</i>

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:32.210
<i>And it was eating away at us silently</i>

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.040
<i>We were so scared that we went numb</i>

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.460
<i>And our legs buckled from under us</i>

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:43.340
<i>We still can't forget the tears</i>
<i>that fell back then even now</i>

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:48.130
<i>Even though we're so frail we might break,</i>
<i>we still continued to seek love</i>

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:53.250
<i>We don't want to forget the reason</i>
<i>we're standing on this stage</i>

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:58.040
<i>Because you're the one who made me stronger</i>

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.500
<i>I give you this lovely ballad</i>
<i>within this beautiful attack</i>

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.670
Seiin High School Boys Volleyball Club
Training Camp Day 1

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.630
Listen up.

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.960
Once we're done with this training camp,
it's gonna be the Fall Tournament.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.420
We're gonna put this team together
in the next five days.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:23.630
I'm sure some of you came here to mess around,

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:28.130
but you best believe I'm gonna work you
to the bone. You better be ready.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.000
Right.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.960
Also, the rugby team member Okuma
that'd been playing with us

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.420
officially joined the team.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.250
He's another second year along
with Kanno, Uchimura, and Hokao.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.170
Okuma, greet everyone.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.130
You got it.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:47.540
Greetings, pleasure to make
your acquaintance, and salutations.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:53.710
Right. We'll take good care of you.
I hope you're ready.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.630
I promise I'll take this seriously. Really.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.000
Coach, could you say a few words...

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:05.670
Let's start practice.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.750
Right!

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:11.850
Episode 4: 'Higher, Faster, Stronger'

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.670
Kuroba!

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.130
You need to put more thought
into where you're hitting.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.420
Right.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.670
Well, Haijima? What do you think of our spikers?

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.790
They're not bad. I think we've got
decent right-side hitters,

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:31.000
so I'd like to increase the number
of middle and right-side combos.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.250
Like A and D quicks,

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.710
A Quick

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.710
D Quick

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.130
and a C quick and a slide hit on the right.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.370
C Quick

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.420
Slide Hit

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.880
Also, a pipe attack with the middle and right.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.380
Aoki, Kanno, Okuma. Gather round.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.460
And Kuroba!

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.420
Right!

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:48.590
Have our left-side hitter practice his receives.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:50.130
You heard him.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:53.040
R-Right...

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.460
Once the middle hitter goes for an A quick,

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.880
our right-side hitter should go for
a D quick that uses most of the court,

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.920
or a time-difference attack would be effective.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.840
In this case...

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.590
Was he like that back in middle school, too?

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.290
Yeah, he was.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:12.210
He's pretty much volleyball personified.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:18.040
But he quickly forgets about
things outside of the court.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.040
He's a bit different on the inside and out.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.500
I'm sure his team will either kill him
or get the most out of him.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:29.540
With those skills, he should be
a top contender anywhere,

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.750
but I guess it's the opposite.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.790
Most teams wouldn't be able to play with him.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:38.090
Being on a bad team would easily break him.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:39.840
Talk about risky.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.960
Right...

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:41.960
But...

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.590
We'll get the most out of him.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:50.000
I made it my mission

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.340
and my responsibility to make sure
his skills get to college.

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:57.500
Senpai...

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.090
All right, next!

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.000
Right!

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.920
Our training camp's five days and four nights.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.130
Two days after that is the Fall Tournament.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.920
It's an important match to work out any kinks

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:15.090
before the prefectural qualifiers
at the end of September, apparently.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:18.540
It'll be our first official match

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.170
since Haijima joined.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.360
Seiin High School Training Camp Grounds

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.170
Let's eat!

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.540
Thanks for the food.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:35.000
Man, I'm stuffed.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.790
I'm beat.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.000
Roger

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.000
You're at your training camp, right?
Good luck!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.040
Roger

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.040
You're at your training camp, right?
Good luck!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:42.000
Itoko? Is that a girl's name?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.590
Is that your girlfriend? Well, is she?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.540
N-No. She's my cousin.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:49.210
She's my cousin named Itoko.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:51.290
Aw, that's no fun.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.710
Get too rowdy and the seniors will yell at you.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:58.500
Must be nice going out with
Suemori from the girls team.

00:06:58.500 --> 00:06:59.340
Huh?

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.250
You're dating her, aren't you?

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.210
What?!

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.840
I saw you two together
at the ball game festival.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:07.340
That's not true at all! Ibara and I...

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:10.630
I mean, Miss Suemori and I aren't...

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:11.540
Haijima!

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.210
What about you?

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.630
I'm single and I always have been.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:20.750
Well, I'm not surprised. You're probably
not interested in that stuff at all.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:24.000
I've had girls that I've liked.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.000
Seriously?! Are they actually human?

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.920
They have arms and legs, right?

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:32.210
I know Vabo- <i>chan</i> has arms and legs,
but they're not human!

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.840
Wake up!

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.710
What are you talking about? Also, why Vabo- <i>chan</i> ?

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:40.090
Vabo- <i>chan</i> ? That's classic, Kuroba.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:43.170
That wasn't a joke, Senpai!

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.000
This is a serious matter.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.960
Seriously, what do you mean?

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.460
All of you, pipe down, and lights out!

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:54.670
Better preserve your energy or
I'm gonna work you so hard until you puke!

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:57.880
If you can't sleep, you can go run up a hill.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:00.040
Okuma, you seem pretty awake.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.960
Nope. I'll be out like a light in a second.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.840
Hey, you awake?

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.920
Go to sleep.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:18.590
So this girl you liked... How long ago was it?

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:20.710
It wasn't while we were at Monshiro MS, was it?

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.540
Go to sleep.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.090
It wasn't Itoko, was it?

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:27.960
Why would you think it's Itoko?

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.920
Did you just call her by her first name?!

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:32.880
Are you still seeing that cousin of yours?

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.210
Seeing-- Wh-What the heck
are you talking about?!

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.880
I'm not seeing her!
And we go to different schools!

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:41.090
She's like a sister-in-law.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:44.420
Sister-in-law? What?

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.960
Oh. By cousin, you mean Yori?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:53.090
I haven't seen Yori forever. Or talked to him.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.170
Then there's no reason to get so mad about it.

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:57.170
That's not why I got mad. I--

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:01.840
Aoki- <i>senpai</i> ...

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:05.710
You two must really want to run up that hill.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.000
Let's make that a reality.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.590
Twenty dashes up that hill!

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:10.840
Right!

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.000
Morons.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.570
Training Camp Day 2

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:17.840
We'll be practicing our
attack formations today again.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.540
We're gonna try out all the patterns
Haijima came up with yesterday.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.240
Got it?

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.290
Yes.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:23.910
Kuroba.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:24.790
Yes, sir!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.000
You can sit out.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.880
There's no point for you to participate,
so just practice your receives.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.920
Wha-- But we're practicing attacks!

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.210
It's not fair for the setter to kick out
a hitter over a personal grudge!

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.420
Personal grudge?

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:43.500
You're probably mad that
we both had to run last night.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:48.420
Like I'd ever make this about that, you moron.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.960
Then why--

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:52.040
You're not needed in today's practice.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:53.000
Why?!

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Kuroba!

