00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.380
Yori!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:23.880
Crap, I'm getting nervous.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:28.090
Don't let your eyes wander. Focus on the court.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:30.210
Everything's on that court.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:32.670
Both our opponents and teammates.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.670
Haijima...

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.100
Shinichiro Oda (3rd year)
Wing Spiker 163 cm

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.100
Misao Aoki (3rd year)
Middle Blocker 193 cm

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.900
Naoyasu Uchimura (2nd year)
Wing Spiker 175 cm

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.900
Akito Kanno (2nd year)
Wing Spiker 181 cm

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.650
Kazuma Hokao (2nd year)
Libero 170 cm

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.650
Yuni Kuroba (1st year)
Wing Spiker 184 cm

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:49.450
Kimichika Haijima (1st year)
Setter 181 cm

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.450
Yusuke Okuma (2nd year)
Middle Blocker 187 cm

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.450
Komi

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.450
Seiin

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.920
Don't panic.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.090
Just wait.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.790
What's wrong?

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:18.090
Yuni hasn't hit a single one yet.

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.670
Kuroba.

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.630
What do you think is special
about Haijima's sets?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.670
They're fast, so they can be an A or B pass.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.090
He doesn't have any notable habits when he sets,

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:32.750
so it's hard for even us to tell
where the set's going to be.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:36.380
Also, if the spikers can't reach his sets,
he acts like it's our fault

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:38.960
yet he still sets up really high.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.250
Haijima's sets are extremely accurate

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:48.840
and customized to fit
each and every hitter's abilities.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.340
Komi

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.340
Seiin

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:56.380
Of course, Haijima's sets challenge
how high the hitters can hit.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:59.000
He'll manage to get you to hit the best

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:00.790
and highest you can.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.170
That's why you get better
when you practice with Haijima.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:08.590
You'll understand that
once we play an actual match.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:11.340
You'll see the court better
than you did in our practices.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.590
You'll have the strength to hit your highest.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:17.250
No one is as devoted as a setter as he is.

00:16:17.250 --> 00:16:19.040
Devoted?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.210
You don't believe in Haijima?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:26.130
It's not that I don't believe in him.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.500
To tell you the truth,

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.920
Haijima told me to keep you
in the game today, no matter what.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:36.130
You just don't believe in yourself.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:38.210
If you can't believe in yourself...

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.840
...try believing in Haijima.

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:48.540
Damn it! Their #2 and #4 blockers.

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:52.340
Just wait.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:00.880
The highest...

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:07.670
...fastest...

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:10.500
...and strongest!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.880
You're the only one who can be our ace.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:18.250
Kuroba!

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.340
That's it!

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:21.380
Ow!

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:26.670
Seiin High has two immovable parts.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.310
Yeah!

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:31.130
The various combo attacks presented
by our setter Kimichika Haijima

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:34.880
and our ace Yuni Kuroba's explosive power.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.190
You did it, Yuni!

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.590
I want people to get to remember
our team because of that.

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:39.880
We'll make it happen, Kuroba!

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:41.040
Right!

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:44.710
Let's turn it up a notch!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:45.710
Right!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.590
This was your plan all along?

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:53.170
I had no choice but to just
set to you in middle school.

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:56.590
Is that why you left me out
of the combo attacks practice?

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.920
You're more than capable on your own.

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:02.630
And we'll draw out your potential.

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:07.210
So they were all in on it.
I'm surprised they agreed.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:11.090
If they cared only about their own reputations,

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:13.210
we wouldn't need them.

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:15.460
I'm going to get you there, no matter what.

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.000
To the Spring Tournament.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.840
You made it sound like this is all on you,

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:24.920
but we're in this together.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:26.090
Yeah.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.000
Another result from our training camp.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.340
Give me the ball, Haijima!

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.960
I won't run away anymore!

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:40.340
I'll break through!

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:42.640
But it is a game, isn't it, Yuni?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.270
Don't tell me you're
actually serious about this.

00:18:47.170 --> 00:18:50.130
I am serious, Yori.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:53.630
I want to play volleyball for real.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:57.170
Everything's on that court.

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:02.840
Both our opponents and teammates.

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:10.040
I didn't think you'd win
both your matches today.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.540
You actually seemed cool, Yuni.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.790
What do you mean, "seemed"?

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.670
Just admit that I was cool.

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:19.630
You still have the semi-finals
and finals, right?

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:23.130
You always get cocky
whenever we compliment you.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:24.340
Yorimichi.

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:28.750
You have something you
wanna say to Yuni, don't you?

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.710
Yeah.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:33.590
So, uh... How was it?

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:36.500
How was it? I don't know.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.670
The venue was pretty chilly.

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:42.340
I thought it'd be hot,
so I didn't feel like going before.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:46.250
Oh, for crying out loud! Just be honest!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:49.000
You wanted to see a volleyball game, didn't you?

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.880
You're interested in volleyball, Yori?

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:52.880
No.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:58.000
I just wanted to see what
you were so obsessed with.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:01.420
For once, you seem to be keeping up with it.

00:20:01.420 --> 00:20:02.840
Keep it up.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.670
Jeez, can you just be honest for once?

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:09.130
Thanks, Yori! I'll do my best.

00:20:09.840 --> 00:20:15.460
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:22.670
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:31.500
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:35.540
<i>The azure world smiles upon me</i>

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:47.920
<i>The knife made up of words from my friend</i>

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:54.840
<i>Still lingers inside my head today</i>

00:20:54.840 --> 00:21:01.000
<i>You glared up at the clouds high in the sky</i>

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:07.460
<i>And near your house, the horizon undulated</i>

00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:14.920
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:22.090
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:31.000
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:39.170
<i>The azure world stabs me strongly in the back</i>

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.630
No way!

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:43.920
Itoko...

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:47.460
B-Brought her boyfriend!

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:51.880
N-No! He's my cousin! He's just my cousin!

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:50.880
He's so tall!

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:53.170
He must play sports.

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:53.170
Must be nice having a boyfriend.

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:56.880
Why would I ever go out with a girl
who resembles an unpeeled onion?

00:21:56.880 --> 00:22:00.090
Maybe if she was peeled...

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.500
Yuni.

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.630
Who are you calling an onion?!

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:11.170
O-Ow!

00:22:11.170 --> 00:22:14.250
You didn't have to hit me with your fist!

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:19.150
I have a match again tomorrow.
What if I got hurt?

00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:21.460
What the hell?

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:23.040
Who do you think you are?

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:23.960
You bastard!

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:26.500
That's enough, you asshole!

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:27.840
Yori?!

00:22:30.590 --> 00:22:31.710
Yori!

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:33.380
Someone stop them.

00:22:33.380 --> 00:22:34.420
Wait, is there a fight?

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:36.210
The hell are you doing here, Yuni?!

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:37.750
Where are you looking?

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:40.500
Who're you? You a friend of his?

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:41.670
Go home!

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:45.460
The hell do you think you're doing?!

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:47.170
B-But...

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:49.460
You won't be able to play volleyball!

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:50.750
Let go!
